<%# Whether a loop is being worked right now, on the toggle itself.

    A loop's card is only visible with the panel open, and the toggle looked the
    same whether the loop was moving or the process holding it had died -- which
    is a question with two very different answers for a reader watching money
    being spent. The mark is the same ring the subagent toggle wears, because
    both say one thing: background work is in flight.

    It is asked of the lease, not of the status word (see LoopLease): a loop's
    file says `active` from the moment it starts until something pauses it, and
    a mark drawn from that would turn forever after the run died. Nothing is
    drawn once nothing is held -- a tick here would claim an ending this panel
    does not outlive: the sheet goes away with the last loop.

    Replaced out of band by the panel's own poll and by every push, because the
    toggle is outside the element those answers target (see
    Web::Loops#loop_state_markup). -%>
<%- running = loops.count { |loop| loop[:running] } -%>
<%- unless running.zero? -%>
<%-   label = I18n.t(running == 1 ? "web.loops.running_one" : "web.loops.running", count: running) -%>
<span class="loop-run" title="<%= h(label) %>" aria-label="<%= h(label) %>"><%= View.spinner_mark("loop-spinner") %></span>
<%- end -%>
